  "principle": "The transmission backbone: TNB operates 132 kV, 275 kV and 500 kV lines. Insulator creepage and clearance are set by the phase voltage and local pollution; the tower type (lattice steel or monopole) follows terrain and corridor constraints; ACSR or AAAC conductors are sized by ampacity and sag; earth wires or line surge arresters protect against lightning, which matters heavily in Malaysia's thunderstorm climate. Live-line working and patrols carry the lifecycle.",
